# Git branch naming - HARD RULE

## Three allowed formats

| Work comes from | Branch name | Example |
|---|---|---|
| A Jira ticket (the default) | The ticket key only: `DOC-XXXX`, uppercase, no prefix, no suffix, no slug | `DOC-2405` |
| A GitHub issue | `issue/{number}-{short-slug}`, slug of 2-4 lowercase words with hyphens | `issue/1845-fastedge-log-field` |
| A contributor draft | `feature-draft/{name}`, a ticket key or a short slug | `feature-draft/DOC-2405` |

```
WRONG:   doc-2405-account-overview-regression
WRONG:   DOC-2405-fix-images
WRONG:   feature/DOC-2405-something
WRONG:   update/some-article
```

For Jira-ticket work the branch is named exactly as the ticket key, nothing else.

## Creating a branch - use the helper script

NEVER run `git checkout -b` manually.
ALWAYS use the helper script from the repository root:

```powershell
.\.agents\tools\create_branch.ps1 DOC-XXXX
.\.agents\tools\create_branch.ps1 issue/1845-fastedge-log-field
.\.agents\tools\create_branch.ps1 feature-draft/DOC-XXXX
```

The script validates the name against the three formats, checks out main, pulls, and creates the branch.
If a skill already created the branch for the current work, stay on it.

## Commit before leaving the branch

The helper checks out `main`. If the current branch is not `main` and it has uncommitted changes, commit them on that branch before running the helper. Stage files by name. Message: `[Product] Short description`.

Never `git stash` to make the switch succeed. The work must show up in `git log` on that branch. The helper refuses to run when the current branch is dirty.

Push and a PR still require an explicit user request.
